    "28": [
        "The Harry Potter movies are based on the \"Harry Potter\" book series written by J.K. Rowling. The series includes seven main books: \"Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone\" (also known as \"Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone\" in some regions), \"Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets,\" \"Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban,\" \"Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire,\" \"Harry Potter and the Order of the Phoenix,\" \"Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince,\" and \"Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows.\" These books served as the source material for the film adaptations.\n\nThe question \"What books are the Harry Potter movies based on?\" specifically asks for the titles of the books that served as the basis for the movies, which are the seven main books listed above.\n\nThe question \"Which books were made into Harry Potter films?\" is asking for the titles of the books that have been adapted into films, which are the same seven books.\n\nSince both questions refer to the same set of books—the seven Harry Potter books that the movies are based on—their answer sets are exactly the same.\n\nTherefore, the most appropriate relation between their answer sets is:\n\n**Equivalence**"
    ],
